<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107935" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρφευ</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερφυῶς</span>
			, <i>excessively, overmuch,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλεόντων δωμάτων ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					377
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐχ ὑ. θνητὸν ὄντα χρὴ φρονεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					820
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί τὴν τυραννίδα τιμᾷς
			ὑ.</span>; <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				550
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρεις ὑ. τὰς τύχας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HF</u>
					1321
				</span></i>
			:—<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> explains it by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεράγαν;</span>
			and in <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				<u>PS</u>
				p.89B.
			</span></i> ( =
			<i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				359
			</span></i>) we have <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδὲν ὑπέρφευ: ἐπὶ τοῦ
				μηδὲν ἄγαν.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
